  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "Done. Rows that land exactly on a half cent were rounding the wrong way. `line_total_cents` in `billing/totals.py` did its math in binary floats. A value like 0.15 at 10% tax should be 16.5¢, but the float came out just under that and rounded to 16¢ instead of 17¢. Python's `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even number, which can cause the same kind of miss.\n\nI switched it to `Decimal` with half-up rounding. I assumed half-up is the rounding you want. The invoice total adds the rounded line totals, so it needed no change.\n\nI added a regression test, `test_half_cent_rounds_up`, in `tests/test_totals.py`. It covers 0.15 at 10%, 0.30 at 15% and 0.35 at 10%. All 7 tests pass with the fix. With the `billing/` change stashed, the suite fails 1 of 7, which is the new test.\n\nReports you already sent out may have wrong totals for rows like these.",
